# Large training / eval tables. Regenerable from Earth Engine, and master_tessera.csv (138 MB)
# blows past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so none of the data tables are tracked. The trained
# .joblib models ARE kept (they're tiny), so the app still classifies straight from a clone.
*.csv
*.npy

# machine-local editor / tool settings + project notes (kept out of the repo)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# scratch / backups
test_data/

# the model zoo is its OWN git repo (pushed to zoo_database.git); not nested inside this one
data/catalogue/

# large downloaded / regenerable artifacts that blow past GitHub's 100 MB limit (wk10):
#   - cod892_biomass: Ratinder's biomass repo (~5 GB of CSVs, keynotes, zips) — reference only
#   - Tessera tiles / tiff cache: ~150 MB each, re-downloaded on demand
#   - the two research PDFs (69 MB / <1 MB) live externally; slides stay tracked
#   - the biomass RF joblib is huge (deep 300-tree forest) — regenerate with scripts/train_biomass.py
cod892_biomass/
global_0.1_degree_tiff_all/
global_0.1_degree_representation/
beyond_flat_classifier_paper.pdf
stacd_paper.pdf
data/refine/biomass_*.joblib

